        "original_id": "10d70157-4f44-5830-8e93-7a1da289c8ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Grohl, Mark Monroe, King Buzzo, Osborne\n- Bands: Foo Fighters, Nirvana\n- Works: Sonic Highways, King Buzzo\n- Topics: documentary miniseries, music history, American cities\n\nFacts:\n- In 2014, Sonic Highways was released as an American documentary miniseries directed by Dave Grohl and written by Mark Monroe.\n- Sonic Highways has eight episodes, and each episode explores the musical history of a different American city through interviews conducted by Dave Grohl.\n- Dave Grohl was the drummer of Nirvana before becoming the founder and frontman of Foo Fighters.\n- In Foo Fighters, Dave Grohl serves as lead vocalist, rhythm and lead guitarist, and primary songwriter.\n- For the project King Buzzo, Osborne recruited Nirvana drummer Dave Grohl.",
